ications of deb. Krystal Biotech, Inc. was founded in 2016 and is headquartered in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Krish S. Krishnan M.B.A., M.S. | Founder, Chairman, President & CEO | Age 60 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 295 people. Revenue per employee of $1.3M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 177%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $640K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $185K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Krystal Biotech, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $9.0B market cap on $389M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +177% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +128.9pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -48% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $189M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 49 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.98\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 14% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 11% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 4.7\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage 